commit 48719e9192ffb8532b726017198ce7e60882bbc0

C03: document.pdf.read reads the text a named PDF carries, minimize-all narration names the plain noun (REOPEN1689)

The owner declared summarizing a PDF with extractable text an expected capability (DECISIONES_DUENO_2026-09-16.md, no OCR). The new read-only operation document.pdf.read (Kernel descriptor, Core handler list, WindowsKnownFileAdapter.ReadPdf) locates the named PDF once in the known folders (desktop, documents, downloads; an ambiguous name is refused, as for the named trash), runs pypdf inside the registered mind runtime as an inline extractor (python -X utf8 -I -c, bounded characters, 90 s, no OCR, no rendering) and returns the text with its counts and hashes. The mind reads «resumime informe.pdf» / «hazme un resumen de informe.pdf» / «summarize informe.pdf» as that operation (file name literal, folder enum owned by the reader), projects the receipt for the composer as the document name, page count, heading-like lines and the opening of the text exactly as read, instructs the report to name the document, its headings and quote its opening verbatim, and vetoes any quoted passage or number the document does not carry (pdf_unquoted_passage, pdf_missing_quote, pdf_unread_number). The known-unsupported contract for PDF summaries lifts by itself now that the operation exists.

The window.minimize.all narration bit now names the plain noun (ventanas / windows): in MINALL1687 the three drafts for «minimizá todo» said «ventanales» and the invented veto rejected them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


